  <note id="note0" x="-116" y="6" color="#fff3b0" text="Campus LANs layer access, distribution and core: access switches dual-home to both distribution switches, and both distribution switches share each floor's default gateway with VRRP (DistA is preferred on floor A, DistB on floor B, so both boxes carry traffic). OSPF over the distribution transit link keeps every return path alive when one distribution switch dies. Try: ping the campus server from a floor PC, then power off DistA and ping again — the PC never touches its settings."/>
